<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jaromar I of Rügen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1218">1218</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jaromar I was prince of Rügen, ruler of the Slavic Rani on the Baltic island of Rügen. After King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-i-of-denmark">Valdemar I of Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/absalon">Absalon</a> captured the temple fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arkona">Arkona</a> in 1168, the Rani princes accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and Danish overlordship. Jaromar succeeded his brother Tetzlav as prince, founding monasteries and building up the Principality of Rügen as a Danish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> state.</p></div>
